Q: How can I apply ellipsis to the text parameter in android compose? A: <p>I can suggest next solution:</p>
<pre><code>@Composable
fun EllipsizeStringParameter(baseText: Int, parameterText: String) {
    val linesCalculate = remember { mutableStateOf(true) }
    val linesCount = remember { mutableIntStateOf(1) }

    Row(
        modifier = Modifier
            .fillMaxWidth()
            .wrapContentHeight()
            .border(0.5.dp, Color(127, 127, 127))
            .padding(8.dp)
    ) {
        Text(
            text = stringResource(id = baseText, parameterText).substringBefore(parameterText)
        )
        Text(
            modifier = if(linesCount.intValue &gt; 1) Modifier.weight(1f) else Modifier.wrapContentWidth(),
            text = parameterText,
            overflow = TextOverflow.Ellipsis,
            maxLines = 1,
        )
        Text(
            text = stringResource(id = baseText, parameterText).substringAfter(parameterText),
            onTextLayout = {textLayoutResult: TextLayoutResult -&gt;
                if(linesCalculate.value ) {
                    linesCount.intValue = textLayoutResult.lineCount
                    linesCalculate.value = false
                }
            },
            softWrap = true
        )
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>where<br />
1. <strong>baseText</strong> is parameter as in your question<br />
2. <strong>parameterText</strong> is string parameter text<br />
3. <strong>main clue</strong> is to separate string in <strong>three single strings</strong> - prefix, middle and suffix<br />
4. <strong>prefix</strong> text is text before parameterText in baseText, <strong>middle</strong> is parameterText itself and <strong>suffix</strong> is text after parameterText<br />
5. and we need to <strong>operate with modifier width</strong> of middle text: if it pushes suffix text to another line we ellipsize it. We can achieve it with <strong>textLayoutResult</strong> of suffix text. Note that we use <strong>linesCalculate</strong> flag to prevent endless recomposition</p>

Q: How to Apply Pagination for Dynamically Created HTML Table in Asp.net MVC A: <p>You can use 'DataTables' jQuery plugin, it is open source and with good API for support.</p>

<p>You need to include jQuery and DataTable plugin like this :</p>

<pre><code>&lt;script type="text/javascript" charset="utf8" src="http://ajax.aspnetcdn.com/ajax/jQuery/jquery-1.8.2.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;script type="text/javascript" src="jquery.dataTables.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>And call dataTable on the desired table :</p>

<pre><code>$(document).ready(function () {           
            $("#dt_basic")
            .dataTable({
               "bPaginate": true,
               "bLengthChange": true,
               "bFilter": true});
      });
</code></pre>

<p>You can do lot more usind Datable like filtering, sorting, pagination, search etc.</p>

<p>Official Site for DataTable - <strong><a href="https://datatables.net/" rel="nofollow">DataTable</a></strong></p>
